# URLs the link checker must not fail on, with a reason for each. An entry here
# is a check switched off, so the list stays short and justified.
#
# These are regular expressions, one per line.

# ACM's DOI host answers 403 to non-browser user agents. The DOI is stable and
# citing it is the point; it cannot be verified from CI.
dl\.acm\.org

# crates.io rate limits automated traffic and answers 429 in bursts. Crate
# existence is already proven by the build resolving the dependency.
crates\.io

# Cloudflare-fronted mirrors of the winget catalogue block datacentre IPs.
winstall\.app

# Requires an authenticated session; always 999 for anonymous requests.
linkedin\.com

# docs.godotengine.org serves a bot-facing 404 for this section before a
# client-side redirect that only a real browser executes (confirmed by eye:
# a NOT FOUND flash, then the page that actually exists). lychee has no
# JavaScript engine, so it only ever sees the 404. Reproduced on two
# different paths in this same section across two separate CI runs
# (index.html, then what_is_gdextension.html), which rules out a one-off
# link, a typo, or a caching fluke.
docs\.godotengine\.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdextension/

# Vigna's personal university page hosting the reference SplitMix64 source.
# It is a single unfronted academic server, and it times out from GitHub
# runners rather than answering with a status code -- lychee treats a
# timeout as a failure and exits 2, so the job went red with zero dead
# links. The URL is cited twice (README.md and docs/DATA-SOURCES.md) and
# resolves fine from a normal connection; the citation stays, the blocking
# check on someone else's uptime does not.
prng\.di\.unimi\.it

# This repository's own compare ranges in CHANGELOG.md. Keep a Changelog
# requires the heading of the version being prepared to link to a diff that
# only exists once that version is tagged, and the [Unreleased] entry always
# points at compare/<newest tag>...HEAD. Between promoting the heading and
# pushing the tag -- which is exactly the window a release PR lives in --
# both URLs are guaranteed 404s, so leaving them checked would make the
# links job fail on every release by design. Only /compare/ is excluded:
# /releases/tag/ links stay checked, so a wrong or missing tag is still
# caught, and the release workflow independently refuses to publish when the
# tag, src/Cargo.toml and the CHANGELOG heading disagree.
github\.com/ZinniXX004/Yet-to-be-JoJo-s-RPG-Game-/compare/
